              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SunnyMixer6046"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The recipe I always use is two parts vodka, one part triple sec, one part Roses sweetened lime juice, shaken over ice then strained into a martini glass. Very delicious! Sometimes I'll kick it up a notch and do three parts vodka. It's a Friday night tradition.",
            "datePublished": "2023-09-26T23:34:54.728Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Heavy_Nutz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The pure unadulterated recipe around the globe \"was\":\n\n2 parts Vodka + 1 part Triple Sec \nw only a splash of Roses Lime- \n\n* I prefer fresh squeezed lemon or lime juice- \n\nIt is a wonderful drink for many, many occasions despite deluding the original recipe weaker- \n\nI recently ordered a double from a local &amp; it was so weak it did not do the name justice- Kamikaze's made correctly will make your taste buds &amp; tongue dance &amp; put a smile on your face in by the 2nd sip- There is another name for the substitution that eludes me where you use tequila instead of vodka- Very tasty indeed.",
            "datePublished": "2020-11-21T22:27:59.277Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
